<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hari Singh Vidyadhar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hari-singh">Hari Singh</a> Vidyadhar was a military commander of the Gajapati Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a> who, according to tradition, defeated a local chief named Dhenka and founded the state of Dhenkanal in 1529. The town and state took their name from the defeated chief. His descendants ruled Dhenkanal as a princely state until its merger with Odisha in 1948.</p></div>
